{
  "id": "ep017",
  "duration": 47.843,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.437,
      "text": "Voyager 2 launched two weeks before its twin, yet was named second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager 2 Launch - GPN-2003-000002.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_2_Launch_-_GPN-2003-000002.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.6,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.6,
          "end": 4.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.437,
      "end": 9.382,
      "text": "Most people naturally assume the lower numbered spacecraft went up first.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager spacecraft (cropped).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_spacecraft_(cropped).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.433,
          "end": 6.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.667,
          "end": 9.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.382,
      "end": 17.427,
      "text": "In 1977, NASA relied on a rare planetary alignment occurring once every 176 years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "72413main ACD97-0036-3.jpg",
        "credit": "Nasa/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:72413main_ACD97-0036-3.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.367,
          "end": 12.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 12.433,
          "end": 17.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.427,
      "end": 23.247,
      "text": "Voyager 1 took a shorter and faster trajectory, reaching Jupiter and Saturn sooner.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager 1 - Jupiter Mosaic - 1979-03-11 (19069026659).png",
        "credit": "Justin Cowart",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_1_-_Jupiter_Mosaic_-_1979-03-11_(19069026659).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.433,
          "end": 23.233,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.247,
      "end": 27.892,
      "text": "Meanwhile, the truly first-launched probe simply took a much slower path.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager final region before interstellar space.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_final_region_before_interstellar_space.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.233,
          "end": 25.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 25.567,
          "end": 27.9,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.892,
      "end": 34.817,
      "text": "That brilliant cosmic detour made Voyager 2 the only spacecraft to visit Uranus and Neptune.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Uranus Voyager2 color calibrated.png",
        "credit": "Ardenau4",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uranus_Voyager2_color_calibrated.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.9,
          "end": 34.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.817,
      "end": 42.067,
      "text": "It discovered hidden rings and dozens of new moons before diving completely south into interstellar space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Neptune Full.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neptune_Full.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.833,
          "end": 38.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.467,
          "end": 42.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.067,
      "end": 47.493,
      "text": "That is precisely why Voyager 2 launched two weeks before its twin, yet was named second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager 2 Launch - GPN-2003-000002.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_2_Launch_-_GPN-2003-000002.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.067,
          "end": 47.833,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
